Add a tick that never waits for the worker thread

tick blocks until the worker has stopped whenever the pattern changed or
the matcher was restarted, whatever the timeout, and otherwise waits on a
timed lock that reads the clock. try_tick takes the worker's lock only if
it is free: while the worker is busy it leaves a pattern change or restart
pending, with the worker asked to cancel, so the next call picks it up;
once it has the lock it does what tick does. A caller polling from a
thread that must never block, such as a UI thread, gets the same results
a call later.

License: MPL-2.0 (nucleo 0.5.0)

